# netsurf: grid-template-columns line names and var() in the -macsurf-grid rewrite (patch 336)
# Generated 2026-10-30
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 335)
#
# grid-template-columns is compiled to `-macsurf-grid: <tracks>` text by
# css_rewrite.c before libcss parses the sheet (MacSurf fixes115/117). On
# developer.mozilla.org the whole page grid collapsed to one column, with
# the table of contents painted over the article. There were three causes.
#
#  - A [line-name ...] list was counted as a track: each bracketed word
#    became a 1fr track. Line names are now skipped in the track emitter
#    (both loops) and in the legacy column counter.
#  - `grid-template-columns: var(--layout-1-sidebar-left)` counted the
#    var() as one track. A var() in the value is now expanded from the
#    custom property's definition in the same sheet: the first `--name:`
#    declaration not inside an `@media print` block (MDN redefines its
#    layouts to one column for print), recursively (4 levels), with the
#    var() fallback when the name is not defined in this sheet. A value
#    that still does not expand keeps the old path.
#  - minmax(<rem|em>, ...) floors were not recognised (only px), so
#    minmax(15rem, 1fr) became a plain 1fr. They now take the 16px root
#    font the rewrite assumes elsewhere.
#  - Bare rem/em length tracks, e.g. the gap track that comes from
#    `var(--gap)` -> "2rem", were emitted verbatim and the -macsurf-grid
#    grammar packed them as px (2rem became a 2px column). They are now
#    normalised to px at the same 16px root font.
#
# Limits (unchanged design): a definition in another sheet, or one that
# depends on a media query other than print, is not seen. minmax tracks
# are approximated by the -macsurf-grid track kinds.
